Reason: entering Asoko (the pirate ship interior) from the earned ship state aborted on cM3dGSph::SetC's range assertion from himo3_control. f28 is only assigned while Link holds the rope, but the hanging rope also subtracts it from its first segment: the GameCube read a leftover FP register, PC read stack garbage (NaN). Initialise it to 0 (full first segment) on PC. Reproduced with the user's checkpoint (probe-OON7Al) and fixed (probe-oxy9bx: Asoko interior, Link in control).

--- a/src/d/actor/d_a_himo3.cpp
+++ b/src/d/actor/d_a_himo3.cpp
@@ -56,7 +56,15 @@
     cXyz spAC;
     cXyz spA0;
     cXyz sp94;
+#ifdef TARGET_PC
+    // Only set while Link holds the rope; the hanging rope still subtracts it
+    // from its first segment. On the GameCube that read a leftover FP register;
+    // on PC it read stack garbage (NaN) and the rope's spheres failed
+    // cM3dGSph::SetC's range assertion on entering Asoko. 0 = full segment.
+    f32 f28 = 0.0f;
+#else
     f32 f28;
+#endif
     f32 tmpReg;
     f32 tmp200;
     f32 f27;
